CORE gnu-extensions
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ existing name: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A clang extension, not ISO C++ (g++ 13 rejects the program, as it does not
implement the attribute).  clang++ 18 accepts this program, and it fails
only its WRONG assertion.  Found while reducing an invoke_result_t failure
with libc++ headers.
